title: Generating the Invoice Importer
type: text/vnd.tiddlywiki

The ''Example Reified Output'' profile reads an OCR-style export in
which every field is its own `{"key": …, "value": …}` object, flattens
it, and makes one tiddler per invoice.  It is a good candidate for an
importer precisely because nobody should have to understand that
flattening twice.  Here it becomes the ''Invoice Importer''.

!!! Check the profile first

# Open the [[Studio]] and click ''Open the Console''.
# Pick ''Example Reified Output'' from the profile dropdown, open the ''Example Reified Output Data'' sample from the sidebar, copy its text, and paste it into the source box.
# Click ''Convert''.  Three invoices stage, none in conflict.  Expand one: `invoice-date`, `vendor`, `total`, a `source-file` field reached through `{{../file_name}}`.

If the staged tiddlers look right, the importer will be right, because
it runs exactly this profile.

!!! Fill in the generator

Click ''Generate importer…'' beside the dropdown.  The generator opens
with defaults derived from the profile; change these:

|!Field            |!Value                                                       |
|Publisher         |your name, lower-case, e.g. `crosseye`                      |
|Slug              |`invoice-importer`                                           |
|Name              |`Invoice Importer`                                           |
|Caption           |`Import Invoices`                                            |
|Introduction      |//Paste the JSON export from the invoice scanner below, or drop the file on the box.  Each invoice becomes a tiddler titled by its invoice number.// |
|Convert button    |`Stage invoices`                                             |
|Sample data       |''Example Reified Output Data''                              |

Leave ''Existing titles'' at //skip//: a re-scan of last month's invoices
should not silently overwrite tiddlers the recipient has since edited.
The ''Studio URL'' is already this wiki's address; every "ask whoever
made this" message in the importer will link back here.

''Screenshot needed:'' the generator form filled in as above, before
clicking ''Generate''.

!!! Generate

Click ''Generate''.  The green box confirms the pack is installed in
//this// wiki, which is the preview: open ''Import Invoices'' from the
link, click ''Try it with the sample'', then ''Stage invoices''.  The
same three invoices stage as in the Console -- but there is no profile
dropdown, no Edit button, and the button says what it makes.

''Screenshot needed:'' the generator's green "Generated" box with its
two download buttons.

The pack also appears on the [[Studio]] page under ''Importers made
here'', and under ''More › Importers'' in the sidebar, exactly as it
will for the recipient.
